prompt:
{
  "public_instructions": "You translate natural-language access-control requirements into Cedar policies using the supplied schema. Cedar denies by default. An applicable forbid overrides every permit. Guard optional attributes with has before reading them. Preserve the schema's entity, set, and attribute types. Use only the supplied task information. Do not use tools, files, search, additional model calls, or external feedback. Produce a single final answer as a JSON object with exactly one field, policy, whose value is the complete Cedar policy text. Do not include explanations or Markdown fences.
",
  "harness": {
    "instruction_blocks": [
      "Translate the access-control requirements into a complete Cedar policy set. Identify each action, eligible principal, resource type, required condition, prohibition, and exception. Use only entity types, attributes, actions, and representations supported by the schema. Implement the stated permissions and restrictions together.",
      "Before answering, check the policy mentally for both unauthorized permissions and missing required permissions. Keep distinct action rules separate when their conditions differ. Apply exceptions only to the restriction they qualify. Return one final policy set."
    ],
    "input_order": [
      "requirements",
      "schema"
    ],
    "checklist": [
      "Every required action is covered.",
      "Role, ownership, membership, and context conditions follow the requirements.",
      "Prohibitions and exceptions compose correctly.",
      "Optional attribute reads are guarded and Cedar syntax is valid."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": "The system manages access to source-code repositories, their pull requests, and their branches for a software engineering organization.

The people involved are developers, reviewers, maintainers, and security leads.

One person may hold both the developer and reviewer role at the same time.

The resources are repositories, pull requests, and branches.

Every repository records its owner, team, sensitivity classification, whether its default branch is protected, its topic tags, and its lifecycle status.

Every pull request records its repository, author, approvers, target branch, approval count, lines changed, whether it requires security review, and its status.

Every branch records its name and whether it is protected.

Each requester carries a clearance level of public, internal, confidential, or restricted, in ascending order of access.

To clone a repository, the requester's clearance level must be at least as high as the repository's sensitivity classification.

A developer, reviewer, maintainer, or security lead must not clone a repository whose sensitivity classification is higher than their own clearance level.

Cloning is only permitted when the repository carries the "regulated-data" topic tag.

A repository that does not carry the "regulated-data" tag may be cloned without this clearance check applying.

Cloning is only permitted when the repository's lifecycle status is active.

A repository that has been archived may not be cloned, even by a requester whose clearance is otherwise sufficient.

A request by a developer with confidential clearance to clone an active repository tagged "regulated-data" and classified as confidential must be able to succeed.",
  "schema": "entity Role enum ["developer", "reviewer", "maintainer", "securityLead"];

entity ClearanceLevel enum ["public", "internal", "confidential", "restricted"];

entity RepositoryLifecycleStatus enum ["active", "archived"];

entity User {
    roles: Set<Role>,
    clearanceLevel: ClearanceLevel,
};

entity Team;

entity Repository {
    owner: User,
    team: Team,
    sensitivityClassification: ClearanceLevel,
    defaultBranchProtected: Bool,
    topicTags: Set<String>,
    lifecycleStatus: RepositoryLifecycleStatus,
};

entity Branch {
    name: String,
    protected: Bool,
};

entity PullRequest {
    repository: Repository,
    author: User,
    approvers: Set<User>,
    targetBranch: Branch,
    approvalCount: Long,
    linesChanged: Long,
    requiresSecurityReview: Bool,
    status: String,
};

action cloneRepository appliesTo {
    principal: [User],
    resource: [Repository],
};
"
}
